# netsurf: <input type=range> and type=color drawn as widgets (patch 223)
# Generated 2026-10-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser 7fc3b8d + patch 222 (patch stack through 222)
#
# Unknown input types fall back to text fields, so sliders and colour
# pickers rendered as 168 x 24 text boxes showing their value, and a
# slider without a value attribute read "" from script.
#
#  - forms.c: range and color make GADGET_HIDDEN controls: their value
#    is kept, synced with the DOM and submitted like a hidden input's,
#    and nothing is edited as text.
#  - box_special.c, box.h: their box is a childless inline-block flagged
#    VB_INPUT_WIDGET.
#  - redraw.c: vb_redraw_input_widget() paints a range as browsers do (a
#    4px grey track, accent-filled up to the value, a 16px round thumb;
#    min / max / value, default 0 / 100 / midpoint) and a color as a
#    swatch of its value inside the box.
#  - default.css: browsers' sizes (range 129 x 16 with 2px margins, no
#    border; color 50 x 27 with a grey border).
#  - vita_polyfill.js: a range input's value is sanitised as browsers do
#    (within min..max, the midpoint when missing or not a number); other
#    inputs are passed through.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/HTML-range-color.html (RANGECOL223, 4 checks,
# Chromium 4/4; before, 0/4): range sizes, margins, the colour well
# size, values and types.
